course: dictionary
lesson: 1230
title: Words about traditions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context helps you work out words that name a show, a place or a tradition. «In a bullfight, a matador waves a cape at the bull.» The words matador and cape are clues: a matador performs in the show, and the cape is the cloth he waves.
explain: The whole sentence explains more than one word. «Bulls cannot tell red from green; it is the cape's movement that makes them charge.» Charge means rush forward at something. Read the whole sentence, not just one word, and the meaning becomes clear.
explain: Some words also show what people think about something. A bullfight is a tradition in some countries, but many people see it as cruel to animals, and some places have banned it. A protest is when people speak out together against something they think is wrong.
fact: A bullfight is a public show in which people fight a bull in a ring.
fact: Bullfights are mainly held in Spain, Portugal, southern France and parts of Latin America.
fact: In most bullfights the bull is killed.
fact: A bullring is the ring where a bullfight takes place.
fact: Many people see bullfighting as cruel to animals, and it is banned in some places.
exercise: «In a bullfight, a matador waves a cape at the bull.» What is a bullfight? | A school sport played with a ball | A race between two horses | A quiet walk through a farm | *A public show in which people fight a bull in a ring
exercise: Many people see bullfighting as cruel to animals. What does cruel mean? | Kind and gentle | Very fast | Loud and noisy | *Causing pain or suffering to others
exercise: «Bulls cannot tell red from green; it is the cape's movement that makes them charge.» What makes the bull charge? | The colour of the cape | The sound of the crowd | *The movement of the cape | The smell of the ring
test: Which country is a bullfight mainly held in? | Canada | Norway | *Spain | Japan
test: In most bullfights, what happens to the bull? | It is given a prize | It is painted red | It goes home to a farm | *It is killed
exam: Which word names the ring where a bullfight takes place? | Matador | Protest | *Bullring | Playground
